__pycache__/

# Build outputs of build_launcher.ps1. The .exe belongs in a release, not in
# the repository: a committed binary goes stale silently and cannot be
# reviewed. launcher.c and the script that compiles it are the source of truth.
obj/
OpenPairings.exe

# Build output of build_installer.ps1: a copy of the repository's own
# top-level LICENSE with a .md extension, so vpk's format-by-extension
# detection renders it. Regenerated from LICENSE on every build - committing
# it would be a second copy of the licence text that could drift from the
# real one.
installer-content/LICENSE.md

# Velopack's own C ABI library, used by OpenPairings.exe for the in-app
# "Install and restart" button (see launcher.c's "In-app updates" header
# section). A pinned, checksummed third-party release asset - CI fetches
# and verifies it in .github/workflows/binaries.yml, the same way
# build_installer.ps1 pins `vpk` itself, not something this repository
# builds or vendors. mix.exs's windows_velopack_dll/1 release step copies it
# from here into the portable payload when present, and skips itself
# (same as a missing Zig) when it is not - see that step's own comment.
velopack_libc.dll
